.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt LIFE_CYCLE-RAND 7ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm life_cycle-rand
.Nd The RAND algorithm life-cycle
.Sh DESCRIPTION
All random number generator (RANDs) go through a number of stages in
their life-cycle:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It start
This state represents the RAND before it has been allocated.
It is the starting state for any life-cycle transitions.
.It newed
This state represents the RAND after it has been allocated but unable to
generate any output.
.It instantiated
This state represents the RAND when it is set up and capable of
generating output.
.It uninstantiated
This state represents the RAND when it has been shutdown and it is no
longer capable of generating output.
.It freed
This state is entered when the RAND is freed.
It is the terminal state for all life-cycle transitions.
.El
